  "question": {
    "text": "The first ionization enthalpy of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Na</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Mg</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Si</mi></math>, respectively, are: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>496</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>737</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>786</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><msup><mrow><mi>mo</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The first ionization enthalpy <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msup><mi>kJmol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mfenced></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Al</mi></math> is",
    "image": null
  },
